You are good enough for for Gehennom but, if this is your
first trip, not for the astral planes. You're carrying way
too much stuff. You want to bring things out of Gehennom,
not take them in. You'll need very little food, for example,
there will be plenty of big monsters to eat, just be sure
not to eat when satiated.

My preferred approach from here is to go down slowly,
squirreling away every item of possible use and cutting
efficient routes between the up and downstairs. Leave one or
two /oDig behind for the plane of earth and try to use the
rest faster than you find new ones. I seldom can. When you
no longer can avoid being stressed, levelport out go to your
stash, unburden, and return to where you left off.

Now continue until you have met and killed Vlad, found the
vibrating square (leave the bell and candelabrum there),
finished all of the wizard's tower except waking Rodney. Now
levelport out again, take the appropriate part of your stash
to the lowest altar and consume all your c?oCM and /oCM
(breaking these at (0:1). Pray every time you get
reconciliation except the last.

Finish buffing and polishing the kit. Grab a /oSDD for the
sanctum, Levelport back to the portal to Rodney's tower.
Kill Rodney with Orcus' /oDeath. Levelport to the bottom Get
the Amulet. On the way out I like c!oGL on no teleport
levels and ?oTele on the others. The speed of the exit cuts
down on your problems.

Ask again if you get this far! :)
